# GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf — Vulnerable OpenSSL bundled in cryptography wheels
# Severity: HIGH (CVSS 7.5) | Published: 2026-06-15
# Fix requires cryptography>=48.0.1, but pan-scm-sdk==0.15.0 pins cryptography<47.
# Tracked: upgrade once pan-scm-sdk relaxes its cryptography constraint.
# Risk acceptance: pan-scm-sdk uses cryptography only for OAuth2 token handling
# over HTTPS; the TLS connection itself is handled by the OS/httpx stack.
GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf

# CVE-2026-69247 (GHSA-g6cj-pr64-35w5 / PYSEC-2026-3552) — Bleichenbacher
# oracle in cryptography's PKCS#7 EnvelopedData decryption
# Severity: HIGH | Fix requires cryptography>=50.0.0, but pan-scm-sdk==0.15.1
# pins cryptography<50.0.0.
# Risk acceptance: only pkcs7_decrypt_der/pem/smime are affected and nothing
# in this codebase calls them (cert import uses PKCS#12, not PKCS#7).
# Tracked: remove once pan-scm-sdk relaxes its cryptography constraint.
CVE-2026-69247
